// Where a document becomes a row of numbers. The deterministic layer's
// own account of what it read, computed from the document and the
// domain's term set and from nothing else, and written beside the
// integer that says what it is comparable with.
//
// THREE LIBRARIES ARE SPLICED HERE AND THE THIRD IS THE ONE TO EXPLAIN.
// src/lib/features.ts builds the vector and src/lib/feature-version.ts
// composes the number stored beside it, which is the pair this group
// was planned around. src/lib/static-gate.ts is here for its hits
// alone: features.ts reads a gate result as a score AND the terms it
// found present, and the category columns are counts of those hits, one
// per category the domain's terms name. That block is the largest in
// the layout and most of what a vector says.
//
// Gate Documents answers gate_score, gate_decision and gate_reason and
// no hits at all, applyStaticGate having spent them on the sentence it
// writes. A vector built from what the item carries would therefore
// store a category block of zeros for every document in every domain.
// That is not a thin vector, it is a wrong one: a zero reads as a count
// somebody took, the version written beside it says the row is current,
// and no recompute ever revisits a document whose version already
// matches. It is the failure documents.features warns about in its own
// column comment.
//
// SO THE GATE READING IS TAKEN HERE, once, over the same body and the
// same term list Gate Documents scored. scoreText is a pure function of
// those two and both are read off nodes above, so a second call cannot
// disagree with the first; what it adds is the hits the first
// discarded. Reading the score back off the item instead would make the
// vector's first column depend on the gate's parking decisions, which
// leave it null for a near duplicate and for an empty body, where a
// vector's first column has to be a reading of the document.
//
// MARKER ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING here and nowhere else on this canvas.
// static-gate.ts and features.ts each declare a top-level function
// asText, which is a redeclaration the runtime accepts and the later
// one wins, so features.ts is spliced second on purpose: its version
// answers the empty string for a value whose string conversion throws,
// and static-gate's lets the throw out. The other order would quietly
// weaken the guard the library that lost wrote for itself. Nothing
// checks this. assertSpliceable in scripts/workflow-markers.ts judges
// each library alone, and a shadowed helper with a different body loads
// without complaint.
//
// THE SPEC IS THE TERM SET AND NOTHING ELSE. FeatureSpec takes a
// quantity roster and a one-hot roster beside the terms and both are
// empty below. DomainSettings in src/db/schema/domains.ts declares
// neither, so reading one off a domain would invent a key nobody wrote,
// and the version is the stronger reason: featureVersionFor digests the
// mechanism and the term set, so a roster arriving from anywhere else
// would move the layout under a number that cannot see it, which is the
// drift this pin exists for. What a domain gets today is the gate
// score, one count per category its terms name, the catch-all beside
// them, and the two text shape columns.
//
// NULL VERSUS ZERO, which the vector answers differently from every
// other reading on this canvas. A feature record cannot hold null.
// Every cell is a finite number by construction, a null or a NaN being
// a cell that trains a model on nothing or crashes whatever reads the
// matrix, so absence is carried by the layout rather than by a value: a
// quantity gets a companion known flag, and a one-hot says nothing was
// stated by having every member AND its catch-all at zero. features.ts
// argues both in full. What reaches this node is the text half, and
// there the zero is measured rather than absent: a document Write
// Documents stored an empty body for is read at length zero, the body
// having been fetched, stored and found empty.
//
// The same rule at the row level is the two columns the statement below
// writes. documents.features is NULL for a document nothing has
// featurized, where an empty object would say a featurizer ran and
// measured nothing, so this node never emits one: the layout always
// names the gate score and the two text columns, so a record built from
// it is never empty whatever the domain holds.
// documents.feature_version is never 0 for the matching reason, and it
// cannot be. featureVersionFor refuses a mechanism version below 1, so
// the smallest number it can answer is TERM_DIGEST_SPAN.
//
// WHY A DISAGREEMENT WITH THE DOMAIN'S VERSION IS LEFT FOR A LATER
// PASS. Load Domain Context carries domains.feature_version for this
// node to hold the composed version against, and the two differ
// whenever the domain's pin was last set under some other
// configuration. Every document this pass writes goes in at the
// composed version, which is the truth about the vectors just computed.
// What this node does not do is walk the corpus. Recomputing the
// documents already stored is a pass over a whole domain rather than a
// step in a capture, and three things put it there rather than here.
//
// A capture pass has to cost what it captured: a run started to read
// one source's page cannot also rewrite every vector in the domain, and
// a node that did would make the price of ingesting anything a property
// of how much had been ingested before. The recompute has to move
// domains.feature_version with it, in one statement over one domain,
// and a pass bumping that pin having featurized only what it happened
// to capture would claim a corpus-wide recompute that did not happen.
// And a document at another generation is not broken: its vector says
// exactly what it said when it was computed, and the version stored
// beside it is the whole of what makes that legible. So the comparison
// travels on the item, the statement below reads it back out, and
// nothing here acts on it.
//
// CARDINALITY. This node GATHERS rather than pairs, which is the first
// time on this canvas that a group does. It is handed one item per
// finding the pass wrote and answers one per document the pass
// inserted, and those are different populations: Apply Call Ceiling
// emits nothing past its bound, so most documents never reached a call
// at all. A document a model was asked about is no more worth
// featurizing than one it was not, and the vector is free and
// deterministic, so the honest set is every document this pass
// inserted, which is what Gate Documents holds. Reading it by name is
// the move every node here makes, the Postgres nodes between having
// replaced the item several times over.
//
// THE VERSION IS COMPOSED BEFORE ANYTHING IS FEATURIZED, and that order
// is deliberate. featureVersionFor refuses a term set it cannot read,
// member by member, so a domain whose rows are malformed stops the pass
// by name rather than storing vectors under a number pinning nothing.
// Composing it first is also what lets it be composed once: it is a
// fact about the domain, and every document in the pass is written at
// the same one.

// The quantity roster and the one-hot roster this domain declares, both
// empty and both named rather than written inline so the paragraph
// above has somewhere to point. A domain that grows either one grows it
// in src/db/schema/domains.ts first, and the digest that pins the
// layout has to reach it before a reader here does.
const DECLARED_QUANTITIES = [];
const DECLARED_ONE_HOTS = [];

// The domain row and its taxonomy, read back off the node that fetched
// them. Every Postgres node between here and there replaced the item,
// so a name is the only handle left.
const context = $('Load Domain Context').first().json;
const domain = context.domain;

// A run id that resolved to no domain, which Load Domain Context
// answers as a null domain rather than as a missing item. There is no
// term set to compose a version out of and no settings to read, so the
// pass stops here rather than writing vectors pinned to nothing.
if (domain === null || domain === undefined) {
  throw new Error(
    '[ar-ingest] Compute Feature Vectors has no domain row: the run '
    + 'this pass was started with resolves to none',
  );
}

// The layout, built once for the pass. The terms arrive with their
// category key already joined on, which is what makes one list serve
// three readers: static-gate.ts takes the pattern, the weight and the
// polarity, features.ts takes the pattern and the category, and
// feature-version.ts takes all four. Load Domain Context selects them
// that way and says so.
const terms = context.terms;
const spec = {
  terms,
  quantities: DECLARED_QUANTITIES,
  oneHots: DECLARED_ONE_HOTS,
};

// The composed version, and the term set's own validation. This runs
// before any document is read for the reason the header gives, and it
// is one number for the whole pass.
const version = featureVersionFor(FEATURE_MECHANISM_VERSION, terms);

// The domain's pin, held against what this configuration composes to. A
// domain nothing has ever featurized carries NULL here, which is a
// disagreement like any other: the vectors this pass writes are the
// first of their generation, and adopting the pin on the strength of
// one capture would claim a corpus nobody recomputed.
const pinned = domain.feature_version;
const matchesDomain = typeof pinned === 'number' && pinned === version;

// One item per document this pass inserted. The gate fields on these
// rows are read for nothing: what the vector needs off them is the
// body, and the reading over it is taken below.
return $('Gate Documents').all().map((item) => {
  const row = item.json;

  // A document the stream cannot name. Mark Near Duplicates drops an
  // item carrying no document id and refuses one it cannot order, so an
  // absence here is the canvas contradicting itself rather than a state
  // to handle. It is worth stopping for because the statement below
  // would not: an update matching no row is exactly what a document
  // carrying no vector looks like, and the two would be
  // indistinguishable in the answer.
  if (row.document_id === null || row.document_id === undefined) {
    throw new Error(
      '[ar-ingest] Compute Feature Vectors was handed a document with no '
      + 'id, which Mark Near Duplicates answers for every row it passes on',
    );
  }

  // The body as Write Documents stored it, which is the text the gate
  // scored and therefore the only text a shape column may measure.
  // Anything else reads as the empty document it is.
  const body = typeof row.body === 'string'
    ? row.body
    : '';

  // The reading, and it is the whole of what the vector is computed
  // from. The same body and the same terms Gate Documents was handed,
  // so the score below cannot differ from the one that node recorded;
  // the hits are what this call is here for.
  const scored = scoreText(body, terms);

  return {
    json: {
      run_id: row.run_id,
      domain_id: row.domain_id,
      source_id: row.source_id,
      document_id: row.document_id,
      features: extractFeatures({ text: body }, scored, spec),
      feature_version: version,
      feature_version_matches_domain: matchesDomain,
    },
  };
});
